# physis-core — what this crate claims it can do, and the two symbols that
# prove each claim runs.
#
#   capability | write path | read path
#
# The rule is `physis-check capabilities`: a capability is present when
# something writes it AND something reads it, both outside the file that
# declares them and outside the test suite. Three capabilities in this crate
# had one half missing (PH-019, PH-021, and the observation watchers) and each
# read as shipped until someone found it by accident. This file is that
# accident, made into a command.
#
# A comma-separated field means any one of the alternatives satisfies that half.

bi-temporal validity        | narrow_until                                                  | is_valid_at
prediction scoring          | resolve_prediction                                            | predictions
structural machines         | StructuralMachine                                             | ProofStatus
continuous observation      | watch_fs, watch_git, watch_shell, watch_agent, watch_proc, watch_browser | read_tail, by_source
acting against belief       | bearing_on                                                    | is_warning
structural map              | build_map                                                     | MapReport
context compression         | compile_context                                               | ContextReport
token-fixed retrieval       | TokenFixedRetriever                                           | ContextReport
interchangeable n-gram table| TableBuilder                                                  | BackoffTable
model provider registry     | NgramDecoderModel                                             | ModelProvider
one configuration mechanism | RunConfig                                                     | load_config
provenance chains           | add_link                                                      | cited_intake_ids
observation to claim        | promote                                                       | cited_by
